PENTA DRAGON DX v3.01
STRUK LABS
=====================

{release_notice}

Penta Dragon DX is a Game Boy Color conversion of Penta Dragon. It adds
scene-aware background and sprite palettes while preserving the original
gameplay, music, story, and stage flow.

Highlights
----------
- Colorized Stage 1, lava treatment in Stages 5 and 7, and individual color
  tables for all nine boss arenas.
- Per-monster colors in normal gameplay and the title-screen spotlight reel.
- Colorized OPENING and final-story artwork with neutral dialogue areas.
- Clean title animation, item-menu HUD, stage cards, death screen, GAME OVER,
  score/level-select screen, and ending pages.
- Exact title footer: DX V3.01 STRUK LABS.

Important title-screen controls
-------------------------------
OPENING START is the first/default option and plays the story introduction.
To begin the actual game, press DOWN to select GAME START, then confirm.

Installation
------------
This archive contains an IPS patch only. It does not contain a ROM.

1. Obtain your own legally acquired Japanese Penta Dragon Game Boy ROM.
2. Confirm that the unmodified ROM matches:
   Size: 262,144 bytes
   MD5:  df43e0adfdc74b2829c7e95e91c71a28
3. Apply Penta_Dragon_DX_v3.01.ips with an IPS-compatible patcher.
4. Confirm that the patched ROM matches the output checksums in CHECKSUMS.txt.
5. Run the result in Game Boy Color mode.

Do not apply the patch to a headered, translated, overdumped, or otherwise
modified ROM. If the output checksum does not match, stop and verify the base
image before reporting a game bug.

Verification
------------
The packaged patch reconstructs the exact ROM that passed all 33 isolated
emulator release gates. Those gates cover the complete title cycle, GAME START
route, stage-card timing and sound, item menu, ordinary enemies, later stages,
all bosses, death/GAME OVER, title-idle reel, both story paths, ending phases,
scroll stability, sound stability, and the live palette workflow.

